Luau's frontend checks modules in parallel when its host gives it a way to
run tasks (Frontend::checkQueuedModules), and two things every check writes
were shared between them. Each check told the frontend's one internal error
reporter the name of the module it was checking, so threads copied names
into the same string; upstream Luau has since given each check a reporter
of its own (FFlag::LuauSplitIceHandler), as this does. And every free type
and error type takes its index from a counter all threads incremented as a
plain int, which upstream still does: the counters are atomic here, relaxed,
since an index has only to differ from the others.

